course: dictionary
lesson: 6207
title: Missionary
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A missionary is a person sent by a church or religion to another place to spread their faith. Missionaries often ran schools and hospitals, or helped people in need. The sentence «missionaries brought schools and writing» is a clue that they did more than teach religion.
explain: Missionary can also describe the work itself: missionary work, or a missionary school. The word after it often tells you what it describes. Test your meaning by swapping it in: "a school run by people sent to spread their faith" still makes sense.
explain: Not all missionary work was kind. The sentence «missionaries brought schools and writing but often banned local customs and languages» shows that. History lessons note that some missionary work was linked with empire and hurt local cultures. Good readers keep both facts in mind.
explain: With missionary zeal is a figurative phrase. It means with very strong, eager belief in an idea. Zeal means great energy and keenness, so someone who talks about a film with missionary zeal wants everyone to see it.
fact: A missionary is a person sent by a church or religion to another place to spread their faith.
fact: Missionaries often built schools and hospitals, and helped people in need.
fact: Famous missionaries include St Patrick, St Augustine of Canterbury and David Livingstone.
fact: «Missionary zeal» means very strong, eager belief in an idea.
fact: Some missionary work was linked with empire and hurt local cultures, so historians study it carefully.
exercise: «Cree syllabics were developed in the 1840s by the missionary James Evans.» What is a missionary here? | A doctor who works in a hospital | A teacher who works only in one school in their own town | A writer who makes up stories | *A person sent by a church or religion to another place to spread their faith
exercise: «Her missionary zeal for recycling means she talks about it all day.» What does missionary zeal mean? | A map of the world | *Very strong, eager belief in an idea | A sleepy, lazy mood | A dislike of rubbish
exercise: «The missionary built a school and a small hospital.» What did the missionary build? | A boat to sail home | A castle on the hill | A church bell tower only | *A school and a small hospital
test: «Missionaries brought schools and writing but often banned local customs and languages.» What does this sentence show? | Missionaries only ever did good | *Missionary work could help people and also hurt local cultures | Local customs were always protected | Missionaries never built anything
test: In «a missionary school», what kind of word is missionary? | A noun, because it names a person | An adverb, because it tells how | A verb, because it shows action | *An adjective, because it describes the school
exam: Which best defines missionary? | A famous explorer who never had any faith | A person who collects old coins | A type of school uniform | *A person sent by a church or religion to another place to spread their faith
